  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of the investigation:\n\n**Root cause:** a startup-ordering race in the new (`MultiCIDRServiceAllocator`) IPAddress-based service-IP repair path, exposed only during mixed-version rolling upgrades.\n\n**Files, in order of the failure chain:**\n\n1. `pkg/registry/core/rest/storage_core.go` \u2014 registers the `start-service-ip-repair-controllers` PostStartHook; its `select`/`time.After(time.Minute)` is what literally emits `\"unable to perform initial IP and Port allocation check\"` if the repair loops don't both signal `onFirstSuccess` within 60s.\n2. `pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/controller/repairip.go` \u2014 `RepairIPAddress.RunUntil`/`doRunOnce`/`syncService`: does an initial reconcile that `Create`s `IPAddress` objects via the loopback client before calling `onFirstSuccess()`.\n3. `staging/.../admission/plugin/policy/generic/plugin.go` and `staging/.../admission/plugin/webhook/generic/webhook.go` \u2014 both `Dispatch()` methods gate on `WaitForReady()` and return exactly `admission.NewForbidden(a, fmt.Errorf(\"not yet ready to handle request\"))` for *any* resource, including cluster-scoped `IPAddress` \u2014 this is what produces `ipaddresses.networking.k8s.io \"...\" is forbidden: not yet ready to handle request`. (Ruled out `namespace/lifecycle/admission.go`'s identical-looking message \u2014 it explicitly skips non-namespaced resources.)\n4. `staging/.../server/hooks.go` \u2014 wires each PostStartHook's completion to a `poststarthook/<name>` healthz check; a hook that returns an error is fatal and its check fails.\n5. `staging/.../server/healthz/healthz.go` \u2014 the `informer-sync` checker, failing on the same underlying informers-not-synced condition.\n6. `staging/.../server/config.go` and `pkg/util/async/runner.go` \u2014 assemble the readyz checks and drive the two repair loops concurrently.\n\n**The race:** the repair-controller PostStartHook fires and immediately tries to `Create` `IPAddress` objects, but the CEL/webhook admission plugins it must pass through aren't ready yet (their own informers haven't synced) \u2014 a strictly later startup step on the *same* newly-started v1.33 process. Every create is rejected as Forbidden until admission catches up. If that doesn't happen inside the hardcoded 60s window, the PostStartHook fails outright, which fails both its own `poststarthook/...` readyz check and the `informer-sync` check, so `/readyz` reports unavailable. This is upgrade-specific because the IPAddress-object repair path (vs. the legacy bitmap-only repair) is new enough that its extra admission dependency wasn't previously on this critical path; once all replicas run v1.33 the timing settles and it stops recurring.",
